---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS, SECURITY_EMAIL } from '../data/moqom';
---

<Base title="Security" description={`Responsible disclosure and bug bounty for elliottwave.studio lab and MOQOM. Report vulnerabilities to ${SECURITY_EMAIL}.`}>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">security</p>
      <h1>Responsible disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        If you’ve found a vulnerability in an elliottwave.studio lab product, we want to hear about it, and we’ll work with
        you to fix it.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`}>{SECURITY_EMAIL}</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#bug-bounty">bug bounty</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>How to report</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`}>{SECURITY_EMAIL}</a> with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>a description of the issue and its impact;</li>
        <li>the affected product, component, version or URL;</li>
        <li>steps to reproduce, or a proof of concept;</li>
        <li>how you’d like to be credited, if at all.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please don’t open public GitHub issues for security reports. <code>security@elliottwave.studio</code> reaches the
        same people.
      </p>
      {/* TODO(Elliott): publish a PGP key or alternative encrypted channel, and link it here and in security.txt (Encryption: field). */}

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We’ll acknowledge your report and keep you updated as we investigate.</li>
        <li>We’ll agree a disclosure timeline with you, and credit you when the fix ships if you’d like.</li>
      </ul>
      {/* TODO(Elliott): commit to concrete response targets (e.g. acknowledge within N business days, triage within N days, default disclosure window). */}

      <h2 id="bug-bounty">Bug bounty</h2>
      <p>
        Our HackerOne program launches as a vulnerability disclosure program. Cash bounties are funded by
        <a href="/donate">donations to the open-source projects</a> until paying customers adopt MOQOM. Until then, every
        valid report gets public credit and our thanks — in the hall of fame and release notes — and we’ll send you
        something: swag in the mail or a tip to your crypto wallet.
      </p>
      {/* TODO(Elliott): LINKS.hackerone is a placeholder until the HackerOne program is live; drop "not live yet" then. */}
      <p>
        HackerOne: <code>{LINKS.hackerone.replace('https://', '')}</code> (not live yet). Until it is, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`}>{SECURITY_EMAIL}</a>. Want to fund the bounty? <a href="/donate">Donate →</a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="hall-of-fame">Hall of fame</h2>
      <p>No reports yet. Valid reports are credited here and in the release notes, if you’d like to be.</p>

      <h2>In scope</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>MOQOM Cloud and its console at <code>moqom.cloud</code></li>
        <li>MOQOM client and server SDKs published by Elliott Wave LLC</li>
        <li>Our websites: <code>moqom.dev</code>, <code>elliottwave.studio</code>, <code>elliottwave.dev</code></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Out of scope</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Denial-of-service and volumetric or load testing against production services</li>
        <li>Social engineering, phishing, or physical attacks</li>
        <li>Accessing, modifying or deleting data that isn’t yours</li>
        <li>Third-party services and components we don’t control; please report those to their maintainers</li>
        <li>Findings without a demonstrated security impact, such as missing headers on static pages, or reports from automated scanners alone</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Test only against accounts and data you own. If you encounter anyone else’s data, stop, don’t keep or share it, and
        tell us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="safe-harbour">Safe harbour <span class="draft-banner">Draft</span></h2>
      <p>
        <strong>DRAFT. We have contacted legal counsel to review this; not yet in effect as a binding commitment.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        If you make a good-faith effort to follow this policy, Elliott Wave LLC will consider your research authorised, will
        not pursue or support legal action against you for it, and will not report you to law enforcement for it. If a third
        party brings action against you for activity that complied with this policy, we will make it known that your actions
        were authorised by us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Good faith means: you avoid privacy violations, data destruction and service degradation; you only interact with
        accounts you own or have explicit permission to test; you give us reasonable time to fix an issue before disclosing
        it; and you don’t use a vulnerability beyond what is needed to demonstrate it.
      </p>
      {/* TODO(counsel): review safe harbour wording (DMCA §1201 / CFAA language, interaction with the player EULA and anti-circumvention terms), and decide whether reverse engineering of binary components is in scope. */}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .draft-banner {
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
